    "updated_at": "2022-06-02T09:07:01Z",
    "body": "I found out what is is,\r\nthis init.nu contains two paths in a more linuxy format,\r\nwhich doesnt work on windows:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlet-env STARSHIP_SHELL = \"nu\"\r\nlet-env STARSHIP_SESSION_KEY = (random chars -l 16)\r\nlet-env PROMPT_MULTILINE_INDICATOR = (^/c/Users/Adrian/.cargo/bin/starship.exe prompt --continuation)\r\n\r\n# Does not play well with default character module.\r\n# TODO: Also Use starship vi mode indicators?\r\nlet-env PROMPT_INDICATOR = \"\"\r\n\r\nlet-env PROMPT_COMMAND = {\r\n    # jobs are not supported\r\n    let width = (term size -c | get columns | into string)\r\n    ^/c/Users/Adrian/.cargo/bin/starship.exe prompt $\"--cmd-duration=($env.CMD_DURATION_MS)\" $\"--status=($env.LAST_EXIT_CODE)\" $\"--terminal-width=($width)\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n# Not well-suited for `starship prompt --right`.\r\n# Built-in right prompt is equivalent to $fill$right_format in the first prompt line.\r\n# Thus does not play well with default `add_newline = True`.\r\nlet-env PROMPT_COMMAND_RIGHT = {''}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI changed it to:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlet-env STARSHIP_SHELL = \"nu\"\r\nlet-env STARSHIP_SESSION_KEY = (random chars -l 16)\r\nlet-env PROMPT_MULTILINE_INDICATOR = (c:\\Users\\Adrian\\.cargo\\bin\\starship.exe prompt --continuation)\r\n\r\n# Does not play well with default character module.\r\n# TODO: Also Use starship vi mode indicators?\r\nlet-env PROMPT_INDICATOR = \"\"\r\n\r\nlet-env PROMPT_COMMAND = {\r\n    # jobs are not supported\r\n    let width = (term size -c | get columns | into string)\r\n    c:\\Users\\Adrian\\.cargo\\bin\\starship.exe prompt $\"--cmd-duration=($env.CMD_DURATION_MS)\" $\"--status=($env.LAST_EXIT_CODE)\" $\"--terminal-width=($width)\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n# Not well-suited for `starship prompt --right`.\r\n# Built-in right prompt is equivalent to $fill$right_format in the first prompt line.\r\n# Thus does not play well with default `add_newline = True`.\r\nlet-env PROMPT_COMMAND_RIGHT = {''}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nand now it seems to work",
